{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"plan\": {\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Retain the approved Core0.1 debt-lowering scope: one explicitly bound source, observation, entity, USD book, interval symbol and DebtMix contract; supported lets, constraints, alternatives and stress scenarios. This is not general Core 0 compilation.\",\n      \"Python 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are available. No installation, network, accelerator, model invocation or delegation is needed.\",\n      \"Package definitions remain separate from caller-supplied evidence. Synthetic acceptance, admission and assumption metadata must be explicitly labeled and supplied; compilation cannot establish human acceptance.\",\n      \"Git metadata is unavailable. Preserve provenance through file hashes and record the unavailable commit identifier without initializing Git.\"\n    ],\n    \"checks\": [\n      \"Performed read-only checks: both modules pass Python AST parsing; borrowing.acc parses into 15 declarations and retains annual-rate units; an added report field is silently discarded. These checks do not establish successful semantic compilation.\",\n      \"Run from the repository root: python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p03.py' -v. Require a nonempty suite and execution of every mandatory case; skips, exceptions and timeouts cannot pass.\",\n      \"Run: python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03. Require actual observations, complete deliverables and nonzero exit on any failed or missing obligation.\",\n      \"Compare independently authored typed and textual programs through complete semantic and binding projections. Verify comments, LF/CRLF and permitted spelling changes preserve semantics while retaining distinct provenance; renamed declarations and changed valid economic inputs must compile without fixture lookup.\",\n      \"Independently calculate one-year interest from evaluated generated fields: P × [alpha × fixed_rate + (1 − alpha) × stress_rate]. Baseline endpoints must give 5/7, a 0.09 stress 5/9, and principal 200 with matching evidence/opening balances 10/14. These are arithmetic checks, not accounting execution.\",\n      \"Exercise malformed syntax, reserved names, invalid dates/escapes, duplicate declarations/fields, unknown names, cyclic lets, missing metadata, ambiguous exports, missing units, invalid dimensions, zero/unproved divisors and unsupported operations through applicable entrypoints.\",\n      \"For each IR corruption, first assert unchanged-schema validity, then require the intended semantic diagnostic. Cover references, arities, quantities, contexts, evidence acceptance/cutoffs, assumptions, package locks/applicability, contract bounds, opening balances, report policies and false family coverage.\",\n      \"Verify input immutability, deterministic compilation, preservation of every branch and global constraint, and absence of expected-fixture reads. Run legacy validation through in-memory APIs only; compare protected-file hashes before and after.\"\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/approved-plan.json\",\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/review_plan-0.response.json\",\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/execution-2/repair-2.process.json\",\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/execution-2/cumulative-changes.json\",\n      \"docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\",\n      \"docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json\",\n      \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\",\n      \"scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py\",\n      \"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\",\n      \"docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"\n    ],\n    \"issues\": [\n      \"The checker, required tests, conformance.json, result.md and progress.md are absent. The latest implementation process timed out after 900.104 seconds despite recording exit_code 0; it provides no successful completion evidence.\",\n      \"Confirmed frontend defect: adding an unknown field to the report declaration produces the same ReportDecl as the baseline. Unsupported source content must be rejected rather than silently discarded.\",\n      \"The documented semantic projection excludes observation display spelling, but semantic_projection currently only removes diagnostics. The comparison contract and implementation disagree.\",\n      \"The case catalog is substantially narrower than the approved checks: it lacks the renamed independent program, most typed counterparts and most semantic corruptions. Existing module size and profile assertions cannot substitute for executable coverage.\",\n      \"Independent validator completeness remains unproved. Inspected code requires targeted checks for duplicate contract fields before dictionary conversion, full package applicability, symbolic contract bounds and exact report-policy binding.\"\n    ],\n    \"next_actions\": [\n      \"Review this remaining-work plan against the original P03 criteria.\",\n      \"Implement the missing tests and checker first, use their failures to repair the existing versioned modules, and produce both actual deliverables.\",\n      \"Submit generated IR, independent expected calculations, semantic rejection results and protected-file checks for result review; retain partial status if any mandatory obligation remains.\"\n    ],\n    \"residuals\": [\n      \"This planning pass changed no files and did not execute a complete source-to-IR compilation or conformance suite.\",\n      \"General packages, events/rules/postings, arbitrary mappings, multiple entities/books/observations, broader currencies/calendars and cross-company concepts remain outside this profile; G2 and G12 remain open.\",\n      \"Extraction uncertainty, accounting elections, estimates, behavior, future innovations, probability measures and general uncertainty admission remain outside this profile; G15 remains open.\",\n      \"Reconstruction, feasibility, accounting validity, empirical forecasting, authoring superiority and human acceptance require separate evidence. All wider MC01–MC35 and G1–G18 obligations remain.\"\n    ],\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"1. Resume the approved implementation rather than rebuilding it. The implementer should first create the missing P03 progress.md checkpoint, record the four existing contributed files and missing deliverables, and hash protected inputs against available phase-entry records. Limit edits to the two versioned modules, profile, case catalog, new checker, required test file and declared P03 outputs/checkpoint. Do not modify controllers, frozen evidence, legacy grammar/schema or benchmark files.\",\n      \"2. Record the revised skeptical audit in the profile before implementation. The baseline remains borrowing.acc plus explicitly corresponding authored-IR fields, excluding reconstruction claims. Primary acceptance requires executable lowering, independent typed equivalence, input sensitivity and semantic rejection coverage together. Schema success, frontend agreement and arithmetic alone cannot promote the result. Unexpected protected-file changes or unavailable dependencies stop affected work; failing cases trigger repair. Missing cases, timeout or incomplete outputs prevent acceptance.\",\n      \"3. Build tests/test_accounting_p03.py and scripts/check_accounting_p03.py early around the existing interfaces. Supply explicit package, reading, opening, report, admission, assumption and alternative bindings without importing expected IR as compiler input. Independently construct typed programs rather than obtaining them from parse_program. Convert catalog entries into executable cases with independently justified expectations, and require every catalog obligation to have an executed result.\",\n      \"4. Repair parsing and frontend preservation. Reject unknown or duplicate report fields and test every other supported declaration for silently ignored content. Preserve source positions, literal spelling, units, exact rational values and normalized semantic strings; test dates, escapes, Unicode, comments and whitespace. Retain typed constructors as a direct entrypoint. Add stable capability diagnostics for recognized unsupported syntax and operations, without treating a schema parser as compilation.\",\n      \"5. Complete targeted shared-semantic repairs exposed by tests. Preserve global constraints in the parent family and branch assumptions only in their alternatives. Enforce name/kind resolution, quantity/context rules, exact evidence-reading equality, acceptance/cutoff metadata, symbol admission, assumption validity, contract principal/opening consistency and report exports/policies. Independently validate schema-valid IR mutations, including duplicate contract fields, symbolic bounds and package coverage of the required period. Reject malformed inputs with diagnostics rather than uncaught exceptions. Preserve Unknown feasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched family cell and no invented witnesses.\",\n      \"6. Resolve the projection mismatch explicitly: compare economically relevant IR and all binding metadata while excluding only documented frontend locations and display spelling. Preserve excluded provenance separately, including raw input hashes. Test semantic equivalence with differing permitted spellings, repeated compilation and immutable inputs. Add a genuinely independent renamed source program, let arithmetic, compound/multiple assumptions, global constraints, changed stress and changed principal with consistent evidence. Keep package-fixed account names as an explicit restriction.\",\n      \"7. Address all prior plan-review residuals in the profile and tests: exact quantity rules, required metadata and comparison projection must be explicit. Audit convenience defaults for perimeter, calendar, horizon and uncertainty kind; require explicit values where omission could silently change meaning, and test renamed entities with matching context. Record each material choice's provenance, justification, failure mode, early diagnostic and status. Retain MC02/MC04 context/provenance, MC10 admission, MC20 package controls, MC23 matched frontend tasks and MC24 language/diagnostic coverage without claiming complete requirement closure.\",\n      \"8. Run the specified checks and repair failures before final reporting. Generate conformance.json from executed cases with complete IR or semantic projections, binding projections, expected/observed outcomes, diagnostics, source/code hashes, requirement coverage and unsupported capabilities. Write result.md with actual commands, environment, wall time, changed files, baseline comparison, decision table, uncertainty and next actions. Separate specification, implemented behavior, tested invariants, accounting validity, forecast validity and human acceptance. Reserve the final interval for these checks and reports; if incomplete, update progress.md with exact remaining failures and return partial status.\"\n    ],\n    \"summary\": \"Resume P03 from its four existing partial files. The approved scope remains appropriate, but acceptance requires missing executable tests, checker and deliverables, plus repairs for confirmed silent report-field loss and the projection mismatch. The plan preserves all original criteria and addresses the prior review's quantity, metadata and comparison requirements.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"PLAN\"\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"The bounded Core0.1 debt profile is the intended P03 target; broader language, mapping, accounting execution and uncertainty support remain later work.\",\n      \"Existing Python 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are available; Git metadata remains unavailable and file hashes are the provenance fallback.\"\n    ],\n    \"checks\": [\n      \"Audited the plan for wrong baselines, proxy promotion, stop conditions, comparison fairness, hidden defaults, stale timeout context, environment mismatch and artifact sufficiency.\",\n      \"Confirmed the plan requires independent textual and typed entrypoints, changed-input sensitivity, renamed source variants, schema-valid semantic negatives and explicit unsupported coverage.\",\n      \"Confirmed the plan explicitly repairs the observed silent report-field loss and semantic-projection mismatch.\",\n      \"Verified the declared dependency versions and inspected the current profile, frontend, IR module, grammar, schema, fixtures and prior process records.\",\n      \"No implementation or deliverable files were changed during this review.\"\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/approved-plan.json\",\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/review_plan-0.response.json\",\n      \"data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P03/execution-2/repair-2.process.json\",\n      \"docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\",\n      \"docs/design/fixtures/p03-lowering-cases-v1.json\",\n      \"docs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc\",\n      \"scripts/core0_frontends_v1.py\",\n      \"scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\",\n      \"docs/design/spec/core-0.lark\",\n      \"docs/design/spec/core-ir.schema.json\"\n    ],\n    \"issues\": [],\n    \"next_actions\": [\n      \"Implement the reviewed checker and unittest suite before final conformance reporting.\",\n      \"Repair any failures involving unknown report fields, complete semantic projection, package applicability, contract bounds, metadata binding or independent case coverage.\",\n      \"Run both required checks and generate conformance.json, result.md and the progress checkpoint;