ars, cross-company concepts, extraction\nscripts/check_accounting_p03.py:136:          'failures':len(result.failures)+len(result.errors),'protected_changes':protection+worker_changes+repair_changes}))\n56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\n57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\n58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\n60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\n61:| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\n67:| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n71:| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\n82:| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n97:| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n99:| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\n101:| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\n116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\n# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Repair execution audit\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Inspection of the\ntimed-out attempt found two partial modules and no tests or deliverables. Its\nsuccessful example compile was insufficient: global constraints were dropped,\nrates were treated as dimensionless, and acceptance, package and domain checks\nwere incomplete. These are implementation failures, not evidence against the\nlanguage design. Repair them before accepting the slice.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Their current hashes are checked\nagainst phase-entry hashes where available, and before/after execution. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\n`not`, compatible addition/subtraction, numeric comparisons, typed equality and\nBoolean composition. Multiplication admits a dimensionless Real or Int factor;\ndivision requires a provably nonzero constant Real or Int denominator. Rates and\nYearFraction are dimensional; rate times money is rejected here (the general\n`simpleInterest` builtin is future work). Integer products remain integer; division\nof scalars returns Real. Addition and comparisons require equal types and compatible\ncontexts. `constant(rate)` is a scenario driver, with a constant, nonnegative annual\nrate. `external(string)` is admitted only for source/opening/report declarations.\nDebtMix principal must equal the accepted debt and opening liability, its fraction\nmust have proven bounds inside [0,1], and component rates must be constant and\nnonnegative. Interval arithmetic proves only conservative bounds; failure to prove\na bound rejects this profile and does not assert mathematical infeasibility.\n\n## Verification and remaining coverage\n\nRun `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_accounting_p03.py' -v`, then\n`python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p03.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P03`.\nThe checker returns nonzero for failed or skipped obligations, includes generated\nIR and binding projections, observations, diagnostics, hashes and runtime details,\nand writes only conformance.json and result.md under the declared output folder.\n\nThe semantic comparison retains IR values, contexts, locks, evidence, assumptions\nand all external bindings. It excludes frontend offsets and observation display\nspelling; those are separately preserved. The authored comparison uses debt value,\ncontext, contract types/fields, assumptions, endpoint conditions, scenario rate,\nopening balances and report policies. Exact one-year interest is checked as\nP * (alpha * fixed_rate + (1-alpha) * stress_rate), using evaluated generated\nfields. At alpha=1/0, P=100 and 5%/7% imply 5/7; 9% stress implies 5/9;\nP=200 implies 10/14. This calculation is not journal execution or forecasting.\n\nMC02/MC04 receive bounded context, evidence and assumption preservation checks;\nMC10 receives factual admission and explicit scenario-assumption checks; MC20\nreceives locked-package and override rejection checks; MC23 receives matched\ntyped/text tasks; MC24 receives parsing, binding, typing and semantic diagnostics.\nNone is wholly closed by this profile. G2, G12 and G15 remain open, as do all wider\nMC01–MC35 and G1–G18 obligations.\n\nUnsupported: general package loading, events, rules/overrides, postings, arbitrary\nreport mappings, records/arrays/field access, finite choices, nonlinear bound\nproofs, implicit conversions, multiple books/entities/observations, dimensions,\ncurrency/calendar variants, rounded or period observations, source conflicts and\nrevisions, cross-company mapping, extraction uncertainty, accounting elections,\nmeasurement estimates, behavior policies, future innovations and probability\nmeasures. Reconstruction, accounting execution, forecast validity, authoring\nsuperiority and human acceptance require separate evidence.\n\n## Current execution evidence contract\n\nThe refreshed approved plan passed skeptical review. Baselines, acceptance and\nstops remain those above; historical controller/P02 changes predate this worker\nand are not worker edits. A snapshot of 370 existing phase-entry files was taken.\nMandatory case coverage is enforced by the checker against the versioned catalog.\nThe paired typed programs are constructed independently of parsing and expected IR.\nMaterial metadata (calendar, horizon, perimeter and uncertainty kind) must be\nexplicit outside the named synthetic demo helper. Their provenance is caller\nevidence, their purpose is reproducible context, their failure mode is silent\ncontext transfer, and omission/renaming tests are the earliest diagnostic. They\nare inputs, not promoted defaults. Exact arithmetic and schema validation are\nengineering diagnostics only. No stochastic or research ranking is undertaken.\n\n## Recovery integrity repair\n\nA fresh nine-method suite passed, but focused schema-valid omission probes found\nthat all assumptions or the report could be removed without rejection. These\nwere validator defects. Mandatory profile cardinalities and model/package/scope\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=json.loads(Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json').read_text())\nfor s in p['plan']['steps']: print(s)\nfor f in sorted(Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03').rglob('*.json')):\n if any(x in f.name for x in ('check','review_result','repair-1.response','implement-0.response')): print('RECORD',f)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=json.loads(Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03/approved-plan.json').read_text())\nfor s in p['plan']['steps']: print(s)\nfor f in sorted(Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T205123-6b8e9a16/P03').rglob('*.json')):\n if any(x in f.name for x in ('check','review_result','repair-1.response','implement-0.response')): print('RECORD',f)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"1. Resume the approved implementation rather than rebuilding it. The implementer should first create the missing P03 progress.md checkpoint, record the four existing contributed files and missing deliverables, and hash protected inputs against available phase-entry records. Limit edits to the two versioned modules, profile, case catalog, new checker, required test file and declared P03 outputs/checkpoint. Do not modify controllers, frozen evidence, legacy grammar/schema or benchmark files.\n2. Record the revised skeptical audit in the profile before implementation. The baseline remains borrowing.acc plus explicitly corresponding authored-IR fields, excluding reconstruction claims. Primary acceptance requires executable lowering, independent typed equivalence, input sensitivity and semantic rejection coverage together. Schema success, frontend agreement and arithmetic alone cannot promote the result. Unexpected protected-file changes or unavailable dependencies stop affected work; failing cases trigger repair. Missing cases, timeout or incomplete outputs prevent acceptance.\n3. Build tests/test_accounting_p03.py and scripts/check_accounting_p03.py early around the existing interfaces. Supply explicit package, reading, opening, report, admission, assumption and alternative bindings without importing expected IR as compiler input. Independently construct typed programs rather than obtaining them from parse_program. Convert catalog entries into executable cases with independently justified expectations, and require every catalog obligation to have an executed result.\n4. Repair parsing and frontend preservation. Reject unknown or duplicate report fields and test every other supported declaration for silently ignored content. Preserve source positions, literal spelling, units, exact rational values and normalized semantic strings; test dates, escapes, Unicode, comments and whitespace. Retain typed constructors as a direct entrypoint. Add stable capability diagnostics for recognized unsupported syntax and operations, without treating a schema parser as compilation.\n5. Complete targeted shared-semantic repairs exposed by tests. Preserve global constraints in the parent family and branch assumptions only in their alternatives. Enforce name/kind resolution, quantity/context rules, exact evidence-reading equality, acceptance/cutoff metadata, symbol admission, assumption validity, contract principal/opening consistency and report exports/policies. Independently validate schema-valid IR mutations, including duplicate contract fields, symbolic bounds and package coverage of the required period. Reject malformed inputs with diagnostics rather than uncaught exceptions. Preserve Unknown feasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched family cell and no invented witnesses.\n6. Resolve the projection mismatch explicitly: compare economically relevant IR and all binding metadata while excluding only documented frontend locations and display spelling. Preserve excluded provenance separately, including raw input hashes. Test semantic equivalence with differing permitted spellings, repeated compilation and immutable inputs. Add a genuinely independent renamed source program, let arithmetic, compound/multiple assumptions, global constraints, changed stress and changed principal with consistent evidence. Keep package-fixed account names as an explicit restriction.\n7. Address all prior plan-review residuals in the profile and tests: exact quantity rules, required metadata and comparison projection must be explicit. Audit convenience defaults for perimeter, calendar, horizon and uncertainty kind; require explicit values where omission could silently change meaning, and test renamed entities with matching context. Record each material choice's provenance, justification, failure mode, early diagnostic and status. Retain MC02/MC04 context/provenance, MC10 admission, MC20 package controls, MC23 matched frontend tasks and MC24 language/diagnostic coverage without claiming complete requirement closure.\n8. Run the specified checks and repair failures before final reporting. Generate conformance.json from executed cases with complete IR or semantic projections, binding projections, expected/observed outcomes, diagnostics, source/code hashes, requirement coverage and unsupported capabilities. Write result.md with actual commands, environment, wall time, changed files, baseline comparison, decision table, uncertainty and next actions. Separate specification, implemented behavior, tested invariants, accounting validity, forecast validity and human acceptance. Reserve the final interval for these checks and reports; if incomplete, update progress.md with exact remaining failures and return partial status.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
