l workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n97:| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
